WEBVTT

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.780
<i>﻿Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.280
The Plavsky particle.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.190
This is the name of a special particle...

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.590
invented by the Plavsky Particle
System Engineering Company, or PPSE.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:35.910
These particles react with the plastic
from which Gunpla is made.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.740
By fluidly controlling the particles,

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:43.550
the normally immobile Gunpla can be
manipulated as the controller wishes.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.120
And through the use of
particle transformation,

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:53.960
effects such as beams, missiles,
and explosions can be reproduced.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:07.870
Any thoughts, Professor?

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:15.110
Are you seriously going to do research
on a particle that only moves toys?

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:20.220
You, the one they call the "Early Genius"!

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.220
Professor, may I speak?

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:27.990
Did you know Plavsky particles are made
by bonding antiparticles together?

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:31.130
I-Is that right?

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:34.470
This technology could be
applied to other fields of study.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:40.640
However, PPSE only uses this
revolutionary particle to move toys.

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:45.480
Besides, the manufacturing method
is kept completely secret.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.180
Either they're scared of their
technology being leaked and misused,

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.820
or there's some other reason.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:54.690
Professor, I...

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:58.920
I have to discover
the secret of this particle.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.690
Hey, Ricardo!

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:40.900
Ricardo Fellini!

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.000
Long time no see, Greco.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.000
Haven't seen you since
the last World Tournament.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.530
Yeah, I guess.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:49.840
What brings you here?

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:51.970
Tomorrow's the final round
of the qualifiers, right?

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:53.640
I came to encourage you.

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:57.580
Guess you have some free time
now that you're in the World Tournament.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:59.750
Don't be sarcastic.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:03.980
If it isn't this year's new model.

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.750
I see, it's well built.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:10.790
I'll pay you back for my losses in
the last two World Tournaments.

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:14.430
Is your opponent Scott?
Or is it Carter?

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.170
No, it's some first-timer kid.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:20.400
Then it'll be easy.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.100
I'm not so sure about that.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:26.970
﻿I hear he only has three months
of experience with Gunpla.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.280
Three months...

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.810
What's his name?

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:34.050
Nils.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:35.980
Nils Nielsen.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:42.690
Greco Logan. Age 27.
20 years of Gunpla experience.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:45.860
Has previously participated
in two World Tournaments.

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:48.430
Top rank is Best 16.

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:51.830
The Gunpla he uses is
the Tallgeese Valkyrie.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:56.570
This machine possesses
high firepower, heavy armor

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:59.810
and more than enough thrust to match.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:05.750
You're fighting in
the Gunpla Battle Championship?

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:09.520
Yes. The best way to get information
about the Plavsky particle,

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:14.560
is to win the qualifiers
and get into the World Tournament.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:19.990
The PPSE works team will also
participate in the Tournament,

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.460
and its founders will be at the venue.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:26.570
If I become a contestant,
I'll be able to meet them...

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:28.700
at receptions and other events.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:34.540
That being said, I'm facing
Mr. Greco in the final round.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:38.210
He's on another level
from my previous opponents.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.880
To compete with him...

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:48.660
I wanted to keep it in reserve
until the World Tournament, but...

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:04.000
Rate of particle motion, 99.97%.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:08.910
Particle compression rate of
energy packs installed in weapons...

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:10.910
is stable at 24%.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:16.880
The high polycaps in all joints
have been successfully activated.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:20.020
No ablation of emotion paint.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:23.820
The numbers underwater are
equal to those on land.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:26.460
It's just as you designed it,
Chief Allan.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:31.030
No, its all thanks to
the PPSE lab's technology.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:34.470
What's more, its fighter
is Meijin Kawaguchi.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:40.740
We're all set for
the World Tournament.

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:42.380
I still have concerns.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:45.280
Is it Nemesis?

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:49.480
Yes. The Gunpla team led by the
methane hydrate excavation king.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:54.390
Rumor has it they're aiming to
make it to the World Tournament.

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:55.360
Is it true...

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:02.560
Sir, Mr. Barthes from the
Flana Institute wants to see you.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:03.700
Let him in.

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:04.830
Yes, sir.

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:12.510
Excuse me, sir.
Let me wish you the best—

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:15.010
Enough pleasantries. Let me see him.

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:18.680
Absolutely, sir. Get in here.

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:27.960
Nice to meet you.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:31.960
My name is Aila Jyrkiainen,
from the Flana Institute.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:35.960
What is this?

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:37.660
What, sir?

00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:42.170
Our Nemesis team asked for
the strongest Gunpla fighter.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:45.440
That's why we invested
big bucks in you.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:48.380
And this is the result?

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:52.450
Aila is the
Flana Institute's masterpiece.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:54.280
She is humanity's
strongest fighter.

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:58.720
Chairman, if you're
skeptical about my ability,

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:01.660
please see it with your own eyes.

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:03.990
I see.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:06.860
Yes, sir.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:09.600
Call Gawain. He has a battle.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:12.930
But she didn't bring her Gunpla.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:16.900
Just use one in the battle room.

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:19.370
If you're humanity's strongest,
you won't mind, right?

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:22.140
Of course not.

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.940
Your opponent is Gawain!

00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:25.210
Never heard of him.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:31.120
He's the main fighter of team Nemesis,
and a world-level player.

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:33.920
Come in.

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:40.590
Gawain, it's battle time.

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:44.230
Huh?

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:46.670
Is Sei still holed up in his room?

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:50.470
I've been telling him to take a break.

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:54.110
But like his dad,

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:56.510
he won't stop
once he gets all fired up.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:00.250
One month until the World Tournament.

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.780
When I won the regional qualifiers,

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:07.590
I assumed the Build Strike Gundam
could compete in the World Tournament.

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:11.090
Reiji battled for me as a fighter,

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:15.130
and the Build Strike was a Gunpla
that I devoted all my energies to.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:20.970
But now it won't do as is.

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:25.070
We lost to Yuuki, contestant in
the last World Tournament,

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:28.980
and to his level of completion,
maneuverability, and firepower...

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:31.750
Reiji and I couldn't match them.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:39.090
When we went to the sea,
we fought that mobile armor Apsalus.

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:45.130
Its I-field reflected particle beams
by altering the Plavsky particles.

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:49.060
That's the true strength of
a world-level Gunpla.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:53.070
And then there was Mao.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:55.500
Even without a super microwave system,

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.600
he fired his hyper satellite cannon.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:04.080
With all of the Gunpla that
fight at a world level...

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:08.380
they understand and apply the
characteristics of Plavsky particles.

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:14.820
I've got to build an original Gunpla
that can face them!

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:43.750
Darn!

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:45.520
Where'd it go!?

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:07.980
<i>﻿Battle ended.</i>

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:12.550
Gawain's Devil Gundam,
defeated by a Jegan...

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:16.680
Wh-Who the heck are you!?

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:20.490
So what do you think, Chairman?

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:21.890
Excellent.

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:25.430
I'll make her the team's main fighter.

00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:27.390
Thank you very much.

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:28.900
But don't get conceited.

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:33.500
That man is also participating
in the qualifying tournament...

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.400
that our team is playing in.

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:38.740
The champion of
the last World Tournament,

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:41.240
Carlos Kaiser.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:44.410
Can you defeat him, Aila Jyrkiainen?

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:48.820
If that is your order.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:53.090
<i>Hey, 6.5 billion Gunpla fans around the world!</i>

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:55.320
<i>The moment of joy has come!</i>

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:59.060
<i>Tonight, here, at the ﻿La Vie en Rose Garden...</i>

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:10.340
<i>This is the final round of
the American regional qualifiers,</i>

00:12:10.340 --> 00:12:13.710
<i>to decide who goes to the Gunpla Battle
Championship World Tournament!</i>

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:17.920
<i>The sizzling match will be brought to you live!</i>

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:20.720
<i>﻿Isn't it exciting?</i>

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:24.150
<i>Of course. ﻿I can't wait.</i>

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:29.120
<i>﻿In this final round, we'll see Greco,
who went to last year's World Tournament.</i>

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:30.760
His abilities are guaranteed.

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:34.430
<i>﻿But his opponent Nils
can't be underestimated either.</i>

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:36.130
<i>﻿Nils is only 13 years old,</i>

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:38.800
<i>﻿and this is his first time
entering the tournament.</i>

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:42.100
<i>﻿Ability in Gunpla Battle
isn't a matter of experience.</i>

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:43.800
So it seems.

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:55.720
He's here!

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:59.950
America's mightiest raging bull!

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:02.690
But, despite his bold nickname,

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:05.030
his fighting style is
subtle and accurate!

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:07.090
The winner of the previous
qualifying tournament,

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:09.900
Greco Logan!

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:15.470
Wow, he looks full of spirit.

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:17.240
He seems resolute about this!

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:18.240
Yes.

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:22.580
Please welcome the challenger
from the opposite side.

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:24.710
He's just 13 years old!

00:13:24.710 --> 00:13:28.080
But having skipped grades and
gone to America's top university,

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:31.520
this young genius has
already earned three Ph.D.s!

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:34.390
His father is
a world-famous detective,

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:36.720
and his mother is
a master of martial arts.

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:42.060
The one-of-a-kind super-boy,
Nils Nielsen!

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:45.800
As always!

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:48.400
It's Nils's famous Samurai Hello!

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:52.270
Influenced by his mother,
he's also familiar with martial arts.

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:56.180
I hear he's a black belt
in both karate and judo.

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:59.110
I can't wait to watch this match!

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:01.950
I've been waiting for this day.

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:05.690
To battle with you, Early Genius.

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:06.450
Thanks.

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:09.120
But you won't reach the World Tournament.

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:12.430
There's a man waiting for me there.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:17.900
I also have a reason not to lose.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:23.100
Well then, let's see
whose feelings are stronger.

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:24.740
Bring it on!

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:29.210
<i>﻿Please set your GP Base.</i>

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:35.050
<i>﻿Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:39.890
The Plavsky particle.

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:43.390
If I can find out the secret
of this particle...

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:46.230
I could...

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:51.160
<i>﻿Field 1, Space.</i>

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:53.570
<i>﻿Please set your Gunpla.</i>

00:15:03.510 --> 00:15:06.450
An improved version of
the Gundam Astray?

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:09.320
He switched machines to face Greco.

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:12.690
How on earth will he fight?

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:22.130
It's become more fun to defeat you.

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:26.070
Tallgeese Valkyrie, launching!

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.240
Sengoku Astray, here I come!

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:35.080
The final round has begun!

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:41.650
That Astray's a close range type.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:43.970
It doesn't have any extra
long range weapons.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:45.470
So...

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:57.920
He's dodging with minimum movement.

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:01.100
Is that what they call "mikiri"
in the martial arts?

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:02.000
In that case...!

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:14.950
Darn!

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:19.150
At full burst!

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:35.700
Th-This is amazing!

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:40.140
The Sengoku Astray is splitting
Greco's beam in half!

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:43.540
<i>﻿I can't believe it.</i>

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:02.200
Greco!

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:10.800
The match is over.

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:11.840
<i>﻿Not yet.</i>

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:20.110
<i>﻿It's not over yet!</i>

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:22.920
<i>﻿Please just give up.</i>

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:24.950
<i>﻿There's no use battling any longer.</i>

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:27.720
<i>﻿I'm being underestimated, huh?</i>

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:30.720
Why are you still fighting,
knowing you'll lose?

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:35.200
<i>﻿I told you. There's a man
who I truly want to defeat.</i>

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:39.100
I can't lose here and now!

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:06.030
At this distance,
you can't use your precious swords!

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:09.130
I'll slam you against the rocks!

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:13.200
<i>﻿It's useless!</i>

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:38.830
Come on.

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:53.340
Wh-What?

00:18:56.310 --> 00:18:57.180
What happened!?

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:01.150
What did you do!?

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:14.160
<i>﻿Battle ended.</i>

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:18.030
B-Battle ended!

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:23.870
Nils Nielsen's Astray has defeated
Greco, the raging bull!

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:25.940
This is unbelievable.

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:28.480
The champion of the
American qualifying tournament,

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:31.980
and the player who'll go to the
World Tournament, has been decided!

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:34.980
The winner is Samurai Boy!

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:37.320
Nils Nielsen!

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:43.160
Greco.

00:19:43.790 --> 00:19:46.560
I didn't imagine the match
would be this one-sided.

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:50.560
Those swords, and that final technique.

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:57.570
That boy makes full use of
the Plavsky particle.

00:19:58.670 --> 00:19:59.410
This is...

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:04.340
a Gunpla built by the new generation.

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:07.250
A reformation, I should say.

00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:10.680
No, it's not just him.

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:11.520
New fighters from around the world are...

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:14.350
Bangkok, Thailand

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:28.180
Buenos Aires, Argentina

00:20:59.470 --> 00:21:00.900
Hey, Sei!

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:03.170
I said, Sei!

00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:05.340
Why are you shouting?

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:06.840
What?

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:10.540
Isn't your Gunpla ready yet?

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:13.180
It's not that easy!

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:14.750
Go away, I need to concentrate.

00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:16.920
What did you say to me!?

00:21:17.820 --> 00:21:19.520
Just...

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:21.590
Leave me alone!

00:22:55.150 --> 00:22:56.850
I'm finally here.

00:22:57.480 --> 00:23:01.050
It was worth coming so far
to watch the battle of...

00:23:01.060 --> 00:23:03.560
the last tournament's champion,
Carlos Kaiser.

00:23:04.160 --> 00:23:05.020
Oh no.

00:23:05.590 --> 00:23:08.290
The final round is about to begin.

00:23:08.300 --> 00:23:09.660
I'd better hurry.

00:23:16.440 --> 00:23:19.470
Wh-What's all this cheering?

00:23:19.470 --> 00:23:21.910
The battle should've just begun...

00:23:23.980 --> 00:23:27.280
Kaiser's Alpha Azieru...!

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:34.190
The world champion, beaten so badly?

00:23:34.520 --> 00:23:37.160
What kind of fighter is that?

00:23:39.690 --> 00:23:43.030
<i>﻿Aila Jyrkiainen of Team Nemesis...</i>

00:23:43.030 --> 00:23:48.970
<i>﻿will represent Finland in the 7th Gunpla
Battle Championship World Tournament.</i>

00:23:51.470 --> 00:23:53.640
I-It's a young lady!

00:23:55.990 --> 00:23:58.590
My Mr. Beargguy III is
challenged to battle,

00:23:58.590 --> 00:24:01.320
and undergoes terrible torment.

00:24:01.320 --> 00:24:03.660
Next episode, "Wings of Imagination".

00:24:03.660 --> 00:24:05.020
Don't miss it!
